  "content": {
    "title": "Raven-Symoné’s Disney Channel Mt. Rushmore Having Lee Thompson, Not Miley Makes Sense",
    "text": "For many millennials in the United States, watching the Disney Channel in the late 90s and early 2000s was like a rite of passage growing up. They would watch shows like Raven-Symoné’s That’s So Raven, Shia LaBeouf’s Even Stevens, Hilary Duff’s Lizzie McGuire, the Joe Brothers movies, Zendaya’s K.C. Undercover, Kyla Pratt’s The Proud Family, and more. That said, it was quite interesting when Raven-Symoné was recently asked by Stepping Into the Shade Room host Thembi Mawema, who is on her Disney Channel Mount Rushmore.In a divisive response, Raven-Symoné noted that herself, Duff, and LaBeouf for sure earned their spots on the list. When Mawema interjected with Miley Cyrus, Raven-Symoné replied, “No, not Miley. I love you, Miley, but not Miley, she came after.”Instead, the That’s So Raven star advocated that Lee Thompson Young from The Famous Jett Jackson earned the final spot on this hypothetical Mount Rushmore. A number of Disney Channel fans weren’t confused by the omission of Cyrus and questioned Young’s placement. Check out a few of the comments found on X (formerly Twitter).Not trying to discredit Raven Simone, but Miley Cyrus is more impactful than her and probably the people on the list. Miley was touring constantly, promoting her show, and she had an even more bigger fame after the Disney era and reached so much success. pic.twitter.com/ujNVGOytGg— Ayman ☭ (I follow back) (@GuyWhoConquers) March 13, 2026Raven-Symoné’s Explanation of Lee Thompson Young on her Disney Channel Mount Rushmore110247139The longtime actress had a great explanation for why Young deserves to be held in high regard as a Disney Channel legend. Raven-Symoné explained:“I would put in The Famous Jett Jackson. He is no longer with us, but he was the first Black show on Disney. So Lee Thompson Young played the famous Jett Jackson, and I believe he should be on Disney Rushmore. He definitely deserves a spot.”For those who don’t know, The Famous Jett Jackson followed the story of a teenage boy who played a secret agent on a TV show, but longed for a normal life back in a fictional North Carolina town. The series starred Young and went on from 1998 to 2001, and was even followed by a TV movie. His Disney Channel tenure predates Raven-Symoné, Duff, LaBeouf, and yes, Cyrus. Additionally, Young was indeed the first Black lead of a series on the network.Raven-Symoné Is Absolutely Correct to Choose Lee Thompson Young over Miley CyrusUsing Raven-Symoné’s explanation alone is enough to justify Young’s placement on the Disney Channel Mount Rushmore. As a kid who watched the Disney Channel, I can say with certainty that I wouldn’t have opened the door to the network’s other original content if it weren’t for the earlier The Famous Jett Jackson. Young’s show, in many ways, was a foundation for Disney branching out and creating its massive list of original programming, which later included Hannah Montana.Speaking of Hannah Montana, Cyrus’ show didn’t premiere until 2006. By then, the Disney Channel was already a well-established and popular network. So, besides being a very popular show among young TV watchers back then and launching the illustrious career of Cyrus as a Grammy-winning singer, I’d argue that Hannah Montana wasn’t as impactful as some may think for the Disney Channel, and that Cyrus’ stardom really is beyond the confines of the kid-friendly network. Along those lines, so are the careers of the Jonas Brothers, Zendaya, and other big star with Disney Channel roots, Keke Palmer.Related: Dwight Howard Announces Retirement and Fans Are Surprised Because of One Major FactThis story was originally published by Men's Journal on Mar 13, 2026, where it first appeared in the News section. Add Men's Journal as a Preferred Source by clicking here.",
